# The root .dockerignore does not apply here.
#
# Docker reads .dockerignore from the root of the *build context*, and the
# server and worker images build with `context: ../../apps/server`
# (deploy/compose/compose.prod.yml). The careful exclusions at the repo root
# govern the web image, whose context is the repo root, and nothing else — so
# a bare `COPY . .` in this Dockerfile was pulling apps/server/.env, which
# holds PP_OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET and PP_SESSION_KEY, and apps/server/data/blobs,
# which on a developer machine is real user file content, into the builder
# stage. None of it reaches the final image (the runtime stages copy only the
# compiled binary), but it is retained in the local build cache and exported
# wholesale by any CI using --cache-to to a registry.
#
# Keep in step with the root .dockerignore.

**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
!**/.env.*.example

# Local blob store and preview scratch — user content, sometimes gigabytes.
data

.git
